{"availability":"available","full":"jackc/jed","name":"jed","description":"Embeddable SQL database","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-27T20:17:51Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:43:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://jackc.github.io/jed/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:14.918Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:14.918Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:14.918Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:14.918Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Embeddable. Capable. Safe for untrusted SQL. One file, no server — types and behavior modeled on PostgreSQL.","jed is an in-process SQL database you link into your program — one database is one file on disk, in the spirit of SQLite. It pairs a broad SQL feature set and a rich type system with observable semantics (NULL logic, comparisons, ordering, exact numerics, errors) modeled on PostgreSQL — the standing rule is match PostgreSQL unless there's an overriding reason (CLAUDE.md §1).","⚠️ Status: 0.x public preview. jed is pre-1.0. Any release may change behavior or the on-disk file format — there are no stability or compatibility guarantees yet, and a database file is only guaranteed readable by the jed version that wrote it. See CHANGELOG.md."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jackc/jed/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5148b30c3783f97a241188a7148b59717592aa86b34e98e5cb5014065440bcf7","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:15.072Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:15.072Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Embeddable. Capable. Safe for untrusted SQL. One file, no server — types and behavior modeled on PostgreSQL.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jackc/jed/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"5148b30c3783f97a241188a7148b59717592aa86b34e98e5cb5014065440bcf7","sourceUr